  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 111 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nFrom Monday into late week, the region will dry out as drier \nmid level west-northwesterly flow develops over the region. It \nshould be noted it will be much cooler this week, with mainly \n60s over the plains for max temps and 50s in the valleys. \n\nBy next weekend, another surge of moisture will move in from the \nPacific and move across the intermountain west, bringing the \npotential for more precipitation to the high terrain. At this \ntime the deterministic GFS is much more bullish than the EC \nwith regard to this system. The statistical guidance products \nstart to show precip developing (mainly snow), especially over \nthe mtns, by next weekend.",
